{"type": "tool_use", "timestamp": 1793896695099, "sessionID": "ses_e536cd8e2ffed8iuQc2jSjRzu9", "part": {"type": "tool", "tool": "knowledge_search_docs", "callID": "call_1bd940e4a09f4357b0294ecb3d991f0b", "state": {"status": "completed", "input": {"query": "Where does AuditService store its audit records database storage", "k": 3}, "output": "[audit-service#Data]\nAuditService: Data\nAuditService stores records in the audit Iceberg table. Records are append-only and are retained for seven years.\n\n[audit-service#Overview]\nAuditService: Overview\nAuditService records every governed data access. Each record holds the caller, the dataset, the columns returned, and the policy decision that allowed or denied the access.\n\n[user-service#Data]\nUserService: Data\nUserService stores users in the users Postgres database. A deleted user keeps their row with a deletion timestamp, so orders and audit records still resolve.", "metadata": {"truncated": false}, "title": "", "time": {"start": 1793896692579, "end": 1793896695057}}, "metadata": {"openai": {"itemId": "fc_05e3c8126b4d8b41016aecb0f47af087d1afde6868cb59edc0"}}, "id": "prt_1ac933b5f001KSLuccslQRhmnJ", "sessionID": "ses_e536cd8e2ffed8iuQc2jSjRzu9", "messageID": "msg_1ac9329f8001FLzedjGTiwEV9p"}}
